invariant: INV-48
file: mlkem_avx2.c
catches: test/docker-aes-runtime-qemu.sh mlkem-avx2
reason: the row sampler takes A's indices where the caller asks for A^T's
  and the other way round, so key generation and encryption each
  multiply by the other's matrix. Only an x86-64 compiler reads the line, so the script builds
  bin/mlkem_avx2_equiv_test for x86-64 and runs it under
  qemu-x86_64. The lane skips without docker, and this then reports
  unguarded rather than caught.

--- old
        x0[j] = transposed ? (uint8_t)i : (uint8_t)j;
        x1[j] = transposed ? (uint8_t)j : (uint8_t)i;
--- new
        x0[j] = transposed ? (uint8_t)j : (uint8_t)i;
        x1[j] = transposed ? (uint8_t)i : (uint8_t)j;
